*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?

# The junit report CI's `pnpm test` step writes (`--outputFile`); produced locally
# by the same command, and never a file anyone wants to commit.
vitest-results.xml

docs/roadmap/

# local scratch
.research/
# The `[patch]` a contributor writes to point `fulcrum-core` at a SIBLING
# checkout of `archimedes-codes/fulcrum` while working on both at once. It must
# never be committed: a committed patch sends everyone else's build to a path
# that does not exist on their machine (cargo fails with `failed to load source
# for dependency`), and it silently defeats the rev pin — the build would use
# whatever the sibling tree holds, not `rev = …` in `src-tauri/Cargo.toml`.
# `.cargo/config.toml.example` (the template) IS tracked; only the live file is
# ignored. See that file for the mechanism and why it is `[patch]` not `[paths]`.
.cargo/config.toml
.cargo/config
# The review workflow's scratch dir (`$PWD/.tmp`: test scratch, Tailwind probes).
# Ignored because Tailwind v4's source detection scans it: a probe file here
# compiles into the shipped CSS (`dist/assets/index-*.css`) unless gitignored.
.tmp/
